	"357": {
		"cId": "357",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Varlaam, Abbot of Khutinsk († 1192)",
			"short": "Venerable Varlaam"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Gal_5:22-6:2",
				"pericope": "213"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_6:17-23a",
				"pericope": "24"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>Thou who, by reclining on earth, fasting and vigils didst put to death every fleshly subtlety,  O Righteous one, and didst appear an inexhaustible stream of healings unto those that with faith hasten to thy relics, O Barlaam, our father; pray thou to Christ God that our souls may be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>As a second Elias, O Father, thou didst bring down rain from the heavens. For he brought down fire and awed the king, but thou didst gladden thy people and didst cause them to keep festival. Great Novgorod is thus greatly praised in thee, having thy relics in it. Do thou keep it unshaken from enemies that we may cry unto thee: Rejoice, O Righteous Barlaam, our father.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
