	"504": {
		"cId": "504",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Gerasimus of the Jordan († 451)",
			"short": "Venerable Gerasimus"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": ""
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Burning with heavenly love, thou didst prefer the harshness of the desert of Jordan * more than all the delights of the world; * hence, a wild beast submitted unto thee even unto thy death, O father, * dying in obedience and grief on thy grave. * Thus did God glorify thee. * And when thou dost pray to Him, O father Gerasimus, ** be thou mindful of us.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"506": {
		"cId": "506",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Erasmus of the Kiev Caves († c. 1160)",
			"short": "Venerable Erasmus"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"508": {
		"cId": "508",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Holy Hierarch Tarasius, Archbishop of Constantinople († 806)",
			"short": "Holy Hierarch"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>The truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, * a model of meekness and a teacher of abstinence * wherefore thou hast attained the heights through humility * and riches through poverty. ** O hierarch Tarasius our father, entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>Having illumined the Church with Orthodox dogmas * and taught all to honor and bow down before the precious icon of Christ, O blessed one, * thou didst denounce the godless decree of the iconoclasts. * Wherefore, we cry out to thee: ** Rejoice, O wise rather Tarasius!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"509": {
		"cId": "509",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Second translation of the relics of Saint Herman, Archbishop of Kazan (1714)",
			"short": "Second translation"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"510": {
		"cId": "510",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Holy Hierarch Porphyrius, Archbishop of Gaza († 420)",
			"short": "Holy Hierarch"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>The truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, * a model of meekness and a teacher of abstinence * wherefore thou hast attained the heights through humility * and riches through poverty. ** O hierarch Porphyrius our father, entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Adorned with thy most sacred ways, * thou wast resplendent in the robe of the priesthood, * O all-blessed, divinely wise Porphyrius; * and thou dost spread beauty by thine exaltations of healings, ** praying unceasingly in behalf of us all.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"512": {
		"cId": "512",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Martyrs Sebastian and Christodulus († c 66)",
			"short": "Martyrs Sebastian"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"518": {
		"cId": "518",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Thalelæus the Hermit of Syria († 460)",
			"short": "Venerable Thalelæus"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"523": {
		"cId": "523",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Basil the Confessor, companion of the Venerable Procopius of Decapolis († c.  750)",
			"short": "Venerable Basil"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>A dweller in the desert, an angel in the flesh, * and a wonderworker wast thou, * O our God-bearing father Basil. * Receiving heavenly gifts through fasting, vigil and prayer, * thou healest the sicknesses and souls * of those who with faith have recourse unto thee. * Glory to Him Who gaveth thee strength! * Glory to Him Who hath crowned thee! ** Glory to Him Who worketh healings for all through thee!</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Receiving divine revelation from on high, * thou didst withdraw from the midst of the tumult, O wise one; * and having lived the monastic life venerably, thou didst receive the power to work miracles and to heal diseases by grace, ** O most blessed and sacred Basil.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
