	"535": {
		"cId": "535",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Saint Gregory the Theologian, Archbishop of Constantinople († 389)",
			"short": "Saint Gregory"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Jn_10:1-9",
				"pericope": "35 (mid.)",
				"cmd": "dow != 0"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "I Cor_12:7-11",
				"pericope": "151"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Jn_10:9-16",
				"pericope": "36"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>The shepherd”s pipe of thy theology * vanquished the clarions of the rhetors; * for beauties of discourse were added to thee * who delved into the depths of the Spirit. ** O father Gregory, entreat Christ God, that out souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>O glorious one who destroyed the rhetors” webs * with the tongue of thy theology, * thou hast adorned the Church with the vesture of theology woven from on high; * and, wearing it, it crieth out with us, thy children: ** Rejoice, O father, thou uttermost mind of theology!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
