	"896": {
		"cId": "896",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Theodore Trichinas “the Hair-Shirt Wearer”, hermit near Constantinople",
			"short": "Venerable Theodore"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": ""
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Thou hast been shown to be all-wondrous in life, O wise father Theodore, and changing thy rags of haircloth, which are more precious than royal treasure on earth, in their place thou didst receive heavenly vesture. Pray thou ever in our behalf, O venerable one.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"897": {
		"cId": "897",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Hieromartyr Ignatius the God-Bearer, Bishop of Antioch († 107)",
			"short": "Hieromartyr Ignatius"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Heb_4:14-5:6",
				"pericope": "311"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Mk_9:33-41",
				"pericope": "41"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>As thou didst share in the ways of the apostles * and didst occupy their throne, * thou didst find thine activity to be a passage to divine vision, * O divinely inspired one. * Wherefore, ordering the word of truth, * thou didst suffer for the Faith even to the shedding of thy blood. ** O hieromartyr Ignatius, entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>The luminous day of thy radiant struggles * proclaimeth beforehand to all Him Who hath been Born in the cave; * for thirsting to delight in His love, * thou didst hasten to be devoured by the wild beasts. ** Wherefore, thou hast been called the God-bearer, O most wise Ignatius.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
