	"1401": {
		"cId": "1401",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Macarius the Great, of Egypt († c. 390-391)",
			"short": "Venerable Macarius"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Gal_5:22-6:2",
				"pericope": "213"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Mt_11:27-30",
				"pericope": "43"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>A desert dweller, an angel in the flesh, * and a wonderworker wast thou shown to be, * O our God-bearing father Macarius, * for having acquired heavenly gifts through fasting, vigilance, and prayer, * thou dost heal the infirm, * and the souls of those who have recourse to thee with faith. * Glory to Him Who hath given thee strength! * Glory to Him Who hath crowned thee! ** Glory to Him Who worketh healings for all through thee!</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>The Lord truly set thee in the house of abstinence * like a star which wandereth not, * guiding the ends of the earth with light, * O venerable Macarius, ** father of fathers.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "2",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>Having in life reached the end of a blessed life * with the choirs of the martyrs, * thou dwellest in the land of the meek, * as is meet, O God-bearing Macarius; * and having populated the desert as it were a city, * thou hast received from God the grace of miracles. ** Wherefore, we honor thee.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
