	"1479": {
		"cId": "1479",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Nativity of Our Most Holy Lady Theotokos and Ever-Virgin Mary",
			"short": "Theotokos"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Gen_28:10-17"
			},
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "2",
				"reading": "Ezek_43:27, 44:1-4"
			},
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "3",
				"reading": "Prov_9:1-11"
			},
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Lk_1:39-49, 56",
				"pericope": "4",
				"cmd": "dow != 0"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Philip_2:5-11",
				"pericope": "240"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_10:38-42, 11:27-28",
				"pericope": "54"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Thy nativity, O Virgin Theotokos, * hath proclaimed joy to all the world; * for from thee hath shone forth Christ our God, * the Sun of righteousness, * Who having annulled the curse, * hath given His blessing, ** and having abolished death, hath granted us life everlasting.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>In thy holy nativity, O all-pure one, * Joachim and Anna are freed from the reproach of childlessness, * and Adam and Eve from mortal corruption. * And, delivered from sin, thy people celebrate it, crying out to thee: ** A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the nourisher of our Life!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
