	"1725": {
		"cId": "1725",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Hieromartyr Pancratios, Bishop of Taoromina in Sicily (1<sup>st</sup> C)",
			"short": "Hieromartyr Pancratios"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>As thou didst share in the ways of the apostles * and didst occupy their throne, * thou didst find thine activity to be a passage to divine vision, * O divinely inspired one. * Wherefore, ordering the word of truth, * thou didst suffer for the Faith even to the shedding of thy blood. ** O hieromartyr Pancratius, entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Thou wast shown to be a brilliant star for the people of Taormina, O Pancratius, * and wast shown also to be a sufferer for Christ. ** Standing now before Him pray thou for them that honor thee, O blessed one.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"1727": {
		"cId": "1727",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Holy Great Martyr and Healer Panteleimon († 305)",
			"short": "Great Martyr"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Lk_21:12-19",
				"pericope": "106",
				"cmd": "dow != 0"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "II Tim_2:1-10",
				"pericope": "292"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Jn_15:17-16:2",
				"pericope": "52"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>O holy passion-bearer and healer Panteleimon, * entreat the merciful God, ** that He grant to our souls remission of transgressions.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "5",
				"body": "<p>Emulating the Merciful One, * and receiving from Him the grace of healing, * O passion-bearer and martyr of Christ God, * by thy supplications heal thou our spiritual infirmities, * ever driving away the temptations of the fœ ** from them that faithfully cry out: Save us, O Lord!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"1729": {
		"cId": "1729",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Martyrs Carpos, Papilus, Agathodoros and Agathonica, at Pergamun († 251)",
			"short": "Martyrs Carpos"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Thy martyrs, O Lord, in their suffering received crowns of incorruption from Thee, our God; for having Thy might they deposed the tormentors and destroyed the powerless audacity of the dæmons. Through their prayers do Thou save our souls.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>As a valuable treasury of the Master And a fountain pouring out streams of healings You gave your relics to those on the earth. Thus they are removing the infirmities of various passions Ceaselessly granting grace to our souls. Therefore, O Divine Martyrs, with one voice we celebrate your festival with love.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
