	"1919": {
		"cId": "1919",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "St. Sampson the Hospitable of Constantinople († c. 530)",
			"short": "St. Sampson"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Gal_5:22-6:2",
				"pericope": "213"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_12:32-40",
				"pericope": "67"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>In thy patience, O venerable father, thou didst acquire thy reward, * having endured in prayer without ceasing, and loved the poor and provided for them. ** Beseech Christ God O merciful and blessed Sampson, that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>Rejoicing with psalms and hymns, O divinely wise and venerable Sampson, * and hastening to thy divine shrine, as to that of an excellent physician and a right acceptable intercessor, ** we glorify Christ Who bestoweth upon thee such grace of healing.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"1921": {
		"cId": "1921",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Prophet Samuel (11th C BC)",
			"short": "Prophet Samuel"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Celebrating the memory * of Thy prophet Samuel O Lord, ** through him do we entreat Thee, save Thou our souls.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>As a gift of great worth given to God before thy conception, * from thine infancy thou didst serve Him, O most blessed one; * and thou wast vouchsafed to declare beforehand the things of the future. ** Wherefore, we cry out to thee: Rejoice, O Samuel, prophet of God, thou great high priest!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
