	"2049": {
		"cId": "2049",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Saint Spyridon the Wonderworker, Bishop of Tremithus († c. 348)",
			"short": "Saint Spyridon"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Heb_13:17-21",
				"pericope": "335"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_6:17-23a",
				"pericope": "24"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>He Who is the truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, a model of meekness and teacher of abstinence. Wherefore, thou didst attain the heights through humility, and riches through poverty. O father Spyridon, entreat Christ God that our souls be saved!</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "2",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>Thou wast shown forth as a champion of the first Council * and a wonderworkerr, O Spiridon, our God-bearing father. * Wherefore, thou didst speak to one dead in the grave, * and didst change a serpent into gold. * And, whilst chanting thy holy prayers, thou didst have angels serving with thee, O most sacred one. * Glory to Him that hath given thee strength! * Glory to Him that hath crowned thee! ** Glory to Him that worketh healings for all through thee!</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Wounded with love for Christ, * and giving wings to thy mind through the radiance of the Spirit, O most sacred one, * thou didst find thy work in thine active divine vision, * O thou that art pleasing unto God, * being a divine oblation, ** and asking divine illumination for all.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
