	"2214": {
		"cId": "2214",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Repose of Saint Theodosius, Archbishop of Chernigov († 1696)",
			"short": "Saint Theodosius"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Jn_10:9-16",
				"pericope": "36"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Heb_13:17-21",
				"pericope": "335"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_6:17-23a",
				"pericope": "24"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>O holy hierarch Theodosius, most honored among hierarchs, thou wast a beacon to thy flock; then thou didst pass on to the mansions of heaven. Pray thou at the throne of the King of glory, that He deliver us from the evils which assail us and save our souls, O holy one, by thine intercessions.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>O holy hierarch Theodosius, for Christ the Chief Shepherd didst thou labor, nurturing thy rational sheep in the spiritual pasture; and from Christ God didst thou receive the gift of healing to cure the spiritual and bodily infirmities of all that with faith have recourse to thy healing relics. Wherefore, pray thou now, O holy one, that all that call upon thy name be saved from the assaults of the enemy, and that our souls find mercy.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"2216": {
		"cId": "2216",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Martyr Theodotus of Ancyra",
			"short": "Martyr Theodotus"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"2256": {
		"cId": "2256",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Theophanes, the Confessor and Hymnographer, Bishop of Nicæa († c. 850)",
			"short": "Venerable Theophanes"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>Preceptor of Orthodoxy, Teacher of piety and purity, Lamp of the universe, Catalyst of the divine spirituality of bishops, O most wise Theophanes, thou hast enlightened all through thy teaching. O, spiritual flute: pray thou to Christ our God, that He may save our souls. </p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>Having thundered the divine incarnation of Christ, Thou didst completely expose the fleshless enemies, O wondrous Theophanes. Therefore, all faithfully and piously cry out unto thee:  Pray unceasingly for us all. </p>"
			}
		]
	},
