	"2587": {
		"cId": "2587",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Great Martyr Marina (Margaret) of Antioch in Pisidia (4<sup>th</sup> C)",
			"short": "Great Martyr Marina"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "II Cor_6:1-10",
				"pericope": "181"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_7:36-50",
				"pericope": "33"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Thy ewe-lamb Marina crieth out to Thee with a loud voice, O Jesus: * \"I love Thee, O my Bridegroom, * and, seeking Thee, I pass through many struggles: * I am crucified and buried with Thee in Thy baptism, * and suffer for Thy sake, that I may reign with Thee; * I die for Thee that I might live with Thee. * As an unblemished sacrifice accept me, * who sacrifice myself with love for Thee ** By her supplications save Thou our souls, in that Thou art merciful.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>Arrayed in the beauties of virginity, O Virgin Marina, * thou wast crowned with imperishable crowns; * and stained with the blood of thy martyrdom, O martyr, * thou hast received the trophy of victory for thy suffering, ** piously shining forth miracles of healing.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"2593": {
		"cId": "2593",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Mary of Egypt",
			"short": "Venerable Mary of Egypt"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Gal_3:23-29",
				"pericope": "208"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_7:36-50",
				"pericope": "33"
			}
		],
		"hymns": []
	},
	"2598": {
		"cId": "2598",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Holy Myrrhbearer and Equal-to-the-Apostles Mary Magdalene (1<sup>st</sup> C)",
			"short": "Equal-to-the-Apostles Mary"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "I Cor_9:2b-12",
				"pericope": "141"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_8:1-3",
				"pericope": "34"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>The honorable Mary Magdalene followed after Christ, * Who for our sake was born of the Virgin, * keeping His precepts and laws. * Wherefore, celebrating thy most holy memory today, ** through thy supplications we receive remission of sins.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>Standing before the Cross of the Savior with many others, * suffering with the Mother of the Lord and pouring forth tears, * the all-glorious one made this offering as praise, saying: * \"What is this strange wonder? Is it Thy will to suffer, O Thou Who sustainest all creation? ** Glory to Thy dominion!\"</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"2630": {
		"cId": "2630",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Saint Nina, Equal-to-the-Apostles and Enlightener of Georgia († 335)",
			"short": "Saint Nina"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Mt_10:1, 5-8",
				"pericope": "34 (mid.)",
				"cmd": "dow != 0"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "I Cor_4:9-16",
				"pericope": "131"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Mt_25:1-13",
				"pericope": "104"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>O Holy Nina, equal of the apostles, minister of the word of God, who emulated the first called Andrew and the other apostles in apostolic preaching, enlightener of Iberia and harp of the Holy Spirit: entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved. </p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Come ye all, and let us hymn today the all-praised Nina, the preacher of the Word of God, the equal of the apostles, who was chosen by Christ, the wise evangelist who has led the people of Kartalinia to the path of life and truth, the disciple of the Mother of God, our fervent helper and tireless guardian.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"2634": {
		"cId": "2634",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Blessed Olga, Princess of Russia and Equal-to-the-Apostles, in Baptism Helen († 969)",
			"short": "Blessed Olga"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Acts_16:12-15, 17:1-4",
				"pericope": "37, 39"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_7:36-50",
				"pericope": "33"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "1",
				"body": "<p>Having furnished thy mind with wings of divine knowledge, * thou didst soar far above visible creation; * and seeking God, the Creator of all, and finding Him, * thou didst receive rebirth through baptism; ** and delighting in the Tree of life, O ever-glorious Olga, thou remainest incorrupt forever.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Let us hymn today God the Benefactor of all, * Who glorified the divinely wise Olga in Russia, ** that through her supplications He might give remission of sins to our souls.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"2637": {
		"cId": "2637",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Paraskeva of Serbia (11th C)",
			"short": "Venerable Paraskeva"
		},
		"scriptures": [],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Having loved the hermetic and silent life, and having longingly run in the footsteps of thy bridegroom Christ, thou didst accept His good yoke in thy tender years. By the sign of the Cross thou courageously fought against the nœtic enemies; through asceticism, fasting, prayer and the shedding of tears, thou didst quench the burning coals of the passions. O Parasceva, worthy of glory: standing now before Christ in the heavenly bridal chamber, together with the wise virgins, pray for us, who honour thy memory.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Holy intercessor of all who are in trouble, let us piously hymn the All-honorable Parasceva: for she rejected the corruptible and accepted the incorruptible way of life forever: therefore she obtained glory, the grace of wonders, by the command of God.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
