	"3111": {
		"cId": "3111",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Martyrs Eustratios, Auxentios, Eugene, Mardarius and Orestes at Sebaste († c. 284-305)",
			"short": "Martyrs"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Mt_10:16-22",
				"pericope": "36",
				"cmd": "dow != 0"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Eph_6:10-17",
				"pericope": "233"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_21:12-19",
				"pericope": "106"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>In their sufferings, O Lord, * Thy martyrs received imperishable crowns from Thee our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * they set at nought the tormentors and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By their supplications save Thou our souls.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Thou hast been shown to be a most splendid luminary, * for those who sit in the darkness of ignorance, O passion-bearer; * for, armed with faith as with a spear, * thou wast undaunted by the arrogance of the enemy, O Eustratius, ** who art far more eloquent than any orator.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "2",
				"tone": "3",
				"body": "<p>Speaking of divine things eloquently before the iniquitous, O all-wondrous one, * thou didst endure beatings with most courageous heart, * didst shine forth with godly signs, * and didst extinguish the towering flame of falsehood. ** Wherefore, we honor thee, O most blessed Eustratius, martyr of Christ.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
