	"4386": {
		"cId": "4386",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "The Holy Transfiguration of Our Lord God and Saviour Jesus Christ",
			"short": "Transfiguration"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Ex_24:12-18"
			},
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "2",
				"reading": "Ex_33:11-23, 34:4-6, 8"
			},
			{
				"service": "vespers",
				"type": "3",
				"reading": "III Kings_19:3-9, 11-13, 15-16"
			},
			{
				"service": "matins",
				"type": "1",
				"reading": "Lk_9:28b-36",
				"pericope": "45"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "II Pet_1:10-19",
				"pericope": "65"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Mt_17:1-9",
				"pericope": "70"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "7",
				"body": "<p>Thou wast transfigured on the mountain, O Christ God, * Who didst show Thy glory unto Thy disciples as far as they could bear it, * May Thine ever-existing light shine forth also upon us sinners * through the prayers of the Theotokos. ** O Bestower of light, glory be to Thee!</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "7",
				"body": "<p>On the mountain wast Thou transfigured, * and Thy disciples beheld Thy glory as far as they could bear it, O Christ God; * that when they would see Thee crucified, * they would comprehend that Thy suffering was voluntary, ** and proclaim to the world that Thou art of a truth the Effulgence of the Father.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"4387": {
		"cId": "4387",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Martyr Dometios of Persia and his two Disciples († 363)",
			"short": "Martyr Dometios"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Eph_6:10-17",
				"pericope": "233"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Jn_15:17-16:2",
				"pericope": "52"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Having struggled in fasting upon the mountain, * thou didst destroy the nœtic hordes of the enemy * with the weaponry of the Cross, O most blessed one. * And thou didst likewise manfully array thyself for battle, * slaying Copronymus with the sword of faith. ** And for both thou hast been crowned by God, ** O ever-memorable venerable martyr Dometius.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "6",
				"body": "<p>Having utterly spurned corruptible things and thoughts * which draw one down to the depths, O venerable martyr Dometius, * thou didst show thyself to be a great leader of monks, * turning to fear the wrath of the king who did not wish to worship Christ as the true God. * Wherefore, thou didst repose, chanting the hymn; ** God is with me, and no one is against me!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
