	"4557": {
		"cId": "4557",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Placing of the Venerable Sash of the Most Holy Mother of God in Constantinople (c 395-408)",
			"short": "Theotokos"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Heb_9:1-7",
				"pericope": "320"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_10:38-42, 11:27-28",
				"pericope": "54"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>O Ever-virgin Theotokos, protection of mankind: * thou hast given to thy city a mighty legacy, * the robe and cincture of thy most honored body, * which have remained incorrupt through thy seedless birthgiving. * For in thee are nature and time renewed. ** Wherefore, we beseech thee to grant peace to thy city and great mercy to our souls.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "<p>Thy precious cincture, which encircled thy womb * which was pleasing to God, O Theotokos, * is the invincible might of thy city and an inexhaustible treasury of good things, ** O only Ever-virgin who gavest birth.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "2",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>Today thy temple doth celebrate the deposition * of thy precious cincture, O all-hymned one, * and it earnestly crieth out to thee: * Rejoice, O Virgin, ** thou boast of Christians!</p>"
			}
		]
	},
