	"249901": {
		"cId": "249901",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Venerable Lazarus the Wonderworker of Mt Galiseia near Ephesus († 1053)",
			"short": "Venerable Lazarus"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Gal_5:22-6:2",
				"pericope": "213"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Mt_4:25-5:12a",
				"pericope": "10"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "<p>With prayerful vigils and outpourings of tears didst thou water thy pillar, * and with sighs from the depths of thy soul thou didst render thy labors fruitful an hun­dredfold. * Thou wast a shepherd granting the petitions of all. ** O our father Lazarus, entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.</p>"
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "4",
				"body": "<p>With gladness the Church of Christ doth glorify thee in psalms as a luminary most great. * Wherefore, cease thou never to beseech Christ, ** that He grant forgiveness of transgressions unto all.</p>"
			}
		]
	},
	"252601": {
		"cId": "252601",
		"name": {
			"nominative": "Saint John the Merciful, Patriarch of Alexandria († 612)",
			"short": "Saint John"
		},
		"scriptures": [
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "apostol",
				"reading": "Heb_4:14-5:6",
				"pericope": "311"
			},
			{
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "gospel",
				"reading": "Lk_6:17-23a",
				"pericope": "24"
			}
		],
		"hymns": [
			{
				"kind": "troparion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "0",
				"body": "In thy patience, O venerable father, thou didst acquire thy reward, * having endured in prayers without ceasing, and loved the poor and provided for them. ** Beseech Christ God, O blessed almsgiver John, that our souls be saved."
			},
			{
				"kind": "kontakion",
				"service": "liturgy",
				"type": "1",
				"tone": "2",
				"body": "Thou didst distribute thy wealth to the destitute, * and hast now received heavenly riches, O John most wise. * Wherefore, celebrating thy memory, ** we all honor thee, O namesake of almsgiving."
			}
		]
	},
